 "summary": "Build percentage skills from simple mental methods to exam-style money, offers, comparisons and interest problems.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "## Finding a Percentage of an Amount without a calculator"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Percent means out of 100"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "When we work out percentages without a calculator we usually start by working out 50%, 10% or 1%."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "50% is the same as 50⁄100  \nWe can simplify 50⁄100 by dividing the top and bottom by 50  \n50⁄100 = 1⁄2"
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "We work out 50% of a number by halving it."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "10% is the same as 10⁄100  \nWe can simplify 10⁄100 by dividing the top and bottom by 10  \n10⁄100 = 1⁄10"
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "We work out 10% of a number by dividing it by 10."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "1% is the same as 1⁄100"
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "We work out 1% of a number by dividing it by 100."
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 1: Work out 50% of £320",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "To work out 50% of an amount we divide it by 2\n\n£320 ÷ 2 = £160  \n50% of 320 = £160",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 2: Work out 10% of £320",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "To work out 10% of an amount we divide it by 10\n\n£320 ÷ 10 = £32  \n10% of 320 = £32",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 3: Work out 1% of £320",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "To work out 1% of an amount we divide it by 100\n\n£320 ÷ 100 = £3.20  \n1% of 320 = £3.20",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
